  "publisher": "Digital Science",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This open dataset has already shown early scholarly uptake, with 2 OpenAlex citations and 4 documented downstream reuses. Its most visible use is in the 2023 preprint and 2024 journal article on beta cell primary cilia, indicating that the data are being drawn into ongoing work on pancreatic cell biology and related ultrastructural analysis.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Figshare dataset provides isotropic 3D electron microscopy data from isolated murine pancreatic islets treated with low glucose. The record is clearly positioned as a reusable research resource rather than a standalone narrative paper, and its metadata show explicit links to related and associated works, including the CellMap 2024 Segmentation Challenge and two referenced publications in cell biology and imaging.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest impact signal is reuse in a focused research thread on beta cell primary cilia. The dataset is cited by both a 2023 bioRxiv preprint and a 2024 Nature Communications article on that topic, and those citations are also reflected in Crossref\u2019s data-citation record. Together, these uses suggest that the dataset is supporting active, cross-institutional work in pancreatic function and diabetes, with relevance to ultrastructural and cell biological analysis.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Beyond citation, the record shows documented downstream reuse and a modest but real usage footprint. DataCite reports 4 views and no downloads, which points to limited direct repository traffic but does not diminish the evidence of methodological or analytical reuse captured elsewhere in the record. The absence of event data in the available public-discourse sources means there is no documented social-media or news-style amplification to report here.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the dataset\u2019s impact profile is one of early but credible scholarly uptake: it is open access, embedded in a challenge ecosystem, and already cited in both preprint and journal literature. The evidence points to specialist reuse in biomedical imaging and pancreatic research, rather than broad public attention. With only 2 citations, the record remains early, but the available signals indicate that the dataset is already functioning as a useful building block for subsequent research.</p>",
